\subsubsection{Running it}

The script needs only [[bash]], [[awk]] and [[canvaslms]], and it is
found as [[ungraded.sh]] is (\cref{sec:cron-ungraded}).
It is run by hand, with our own credentials, so none of the care that a
[[cron]] job needs applies here.

A program that knows a course's renames can keep its rules in a file of
its own and pass it with [[-r]], or install it as our own file.
To test such rules without Canvas, it can source the script and call
[[carryover_plan]] on the six files of \cref{sec:carryover-plan}, as the
tests above do:
\begin{minted}{bash}
source "$(python3 -c 'import canvaslms, pathlib
print(pathlib.Path(canvaslms.__file__).parent / "scripts" / "carryover.sh")')"
carryover_plan "$dir" 67592 DD2520
\end{minted}
